You've got full authority to butcher them!

261
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:39,217
Protecting me is your
one and only priority.

262
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:40,640
Got it?

263
00:16:41,620 --> 00:16:42,660
Where's Funfrey?

264
00:16:54,980 --> 00:16:56,600
There, good boy.

265
00:17:00,360 --> 00:17:04,560
I've got CP9 on my side, and I've
got my trusty elephant sword.

266
00:17:04,820 --> 00:17:08,557
As long as I maintain my cool,
there's nothing that can stop me.

267
00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:10,597
Now, we're off to the Gates of Justice.

268
00:17:10,680 --> 00:17:14,757
If you really think you can take this woman
from me, go ahead and try it, Straw Hat!

269
00:17:14,840 --> 00:17:16,720
Big Bro Franky is alive!

270
00:17:16,980 --> 00:17:19,274
The Straw Hats actually made it across!

271
00:17:19,620 --> 00:17:21,400
They finally did it!

272
00:17:21,660 --> 00:17:23,360
Big Bro is free at last!

273
00:17:23,540 --> 00:17:24,957
And he's gonna join the fight!

274
00:17:25,040 --> 00:17:25,870
Hell yeah!

275
00:17:25,953 --> 00:17:27,437
Our bro is one hell of a guy!

276
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:28,920
Go get him, Franky!

277
00:17:29,960 --> 00:17:31,080
Take him down!

278
00:17:31,320 --> 00:17:32,780
Go Straw Hats!

279
00:17:33,020 --> 00:17:35,780
The rest is in your hands, Straw Hats!

280
00:17:38,560 --> 00:17:40,460
Hey, talk to me! You guys okay?

281
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:41,917
Come on, you old hag!

282
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:44,877
Start moving and just what the
hell do you think you're doing?

283
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:48,137
Pulling a flat-out stupid stunt
with Rocket Man like that?

284
00:17:48,220 --> 00:17:50,396
I mean, thanks for saving us and all.

285
00:17:50,700 --> 00:17:52,640
Hey, you hear me? Get up!

286
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:54,400
Please, don't die!

287
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:56,380
Don't die, you old hag!

288
00:18:10,460 --> 00:18:11,417
Bloody gongers!

289
00:18:11,500 --> 00:18:14,676
You're damn lucky, you bloody
nose, is all you've got!

290
00:18:15,140 --> 00:18:15,980
Oh, boy!

291
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:17,200
We made it!

292
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:19,900
Guess he's fine.

293
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:23,229
Thanks for the ride
across, Monster Granny!

294
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:25,700
Come on, you guys, get up already!

295
00:18:26,020 --> 00:18:28,138
You've been through worse than that!

296
00:18:29,020 --> 00:18:31,260
Oh, sure, that's easy for you to say.

297
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:33,009
You're made out of rubber.

298
00:18:33,120 --> 00:18:37,002
We're lucky we're not in pieces
right now after a crash like that.

299
00:18:42,640 --> 00:18:44,169
See, you're all just fine.

300
00:18:44,380 --> 00:18:46,880
You know, you guys are a bunch of weirdos.

301
00:18:47,100 --> 00:18:48,617
It felt like I should point that out.

302
00:18:48,700 --> 00:18:50,277
There's a staircase over there.

303
00:18:50,360 --> 00:18:53,066
We'd better move it if
we're gonna find Robin.

304
00:18:59,500 --> 00:19:00,760
Not so fast!

305
00:19:02,740 --> 00:19:04,220
What the hell is that?

306
00:19:05,860 --> 00:19:08,160
So you've invaded the Tower of Law.

307
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:10,297
There's no point in going on.

308
00:19:10,380 --> 00:19:12,300
You won't ever find Nico Robin.

309
00:19:12,640 --> 00:19:15,581
Luchi's already taken her
to the Gates of Justice.

310
00:19:16,340 --> 00:19:18,760
Oh, and the chief's with them, too.

311
00:19:20,600 --> 00:19:21,480
Hmm. Really?

312
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:24,859
Thanks for telling us where
we should start looking.

313
00:19:25,520 --> 00:19:27,600
Chababa, why'd I tell them that?

314
00:19:27,780 --> 00:19:29,040
He's not too bright.

315
00:19:29,420 --> 00:19:30,740
It doesn't matter.

316
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:32,937
I might have told you
where they're headed,

317
00:19:33,020 --> 00:19:34,997
but I'm not gonna tell
you how to get there?

318
00:19:35,080 --> 00:19:37,537
and you'll never make
it past our CP9 agents.

319
00:19:37,620 --> 00:19:41,091
We've been given direct orders
to eliminate you, Chapa-Bah.

320
00:19:41,340 --> 00:19:43,320
Did he say eliminate us?

321
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:45,040
You want Nico Robin?

322
00:19:45,300 --> 00:19:47,437
Then you're gonna have to
fight your way through each

323
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:49,877
and every one of our agents
if you want to succeed.

324
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:50,790
Duh!

325
00:19:50,873 --> 00:19:53,477
I liked it better when you were telling
us things we didn't already know.

326
00:19:53,560 --> 00:19:56,320
Chapa-Bah, you've got some fire in you.

327
00:19:56,640 --> 00:20:00,880
But I've got one more thing to
tell you. Say it. We're listening.

328
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:03,200
Uh, well, thank you.

329
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,680
Now, give me just a sec.

330
00:20:06,320 --> 00:20:07,720
Take a look at this.

331
00:20:08,060 --> 00:20:08,900
A key?

332
00:20:09,460 --> 00:20:10,440
What's it for?

333
00:20:11,160 --> 00:20:12,320
For all you know,

334
00:20:12,500 --> 00:20:16,817
it might be the key needed to unlock
Nico Robin's C-PRISM Stone handcuffs.

335
00:20:16,900 --> 00:20:18,000
C-PRISM Stone?

336
00:20:18,240 --> 00:20:21,677
It's a stone that nullifies a
person's Devil Fruit abilities.

337
00:20:21,760 --> 00:20:24,757
It's basically the same as
when they fall into the ocean.

338
00:20:24,840 --> 00:20:27,977
Well, now we finally know why
Robin hasn't been fighting back.

339
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:29,740
I knew it wasn't adding up.

340
00:20:29,880 --> 00:20:32,457
Yeah, she's not the
type to give up so easy.

341
00:20:32,540 --> 00:20:36,457
I'm sure she'd be mopping the floor with
their ugly mugs if she had the choice.

342
00:20:36,540 --> 00:20:38,069
She must feel so helpless.

343
00:20:38,760 --> 00:20:39,760
Well, that sucks.

344
00:20:40,060 --> 00:20:44,357
Even if you were able to get past us
and save her in some imaginary world,

345
00:20:44,440 --> 00:20:47,017
that C-prism stone is
tougher than a diamond.

346
00:20:47,100 --> 00:20:51,100
She'd have to live with them on her
wrists for the rest of her life.

347
00:20:51,720 --> 00:20:54,100
Why do I keep telling them this stuff?

348
00:20:54,440 --> 00:20:56,400
He really is dumb, isn't he?

349
00:20:56,640 --> 00:20:57,880
So be my guest.

350
00:20:58,060 --> 00:21:00,413
Go try to save her if you think you can.

351
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:04,150
Fuck!

352
00:21:04,600 --> 00:21:06,180
Give me that key!

353
00:21:12,080 --> 00:21:14,820
Guess all the CP9 guys can use that move.

354
00:21:15,320 --> 00:21:16,700
Don't be hasty.

355
00:21:16,860 --> 00:21:20,237
You don't even know if this is
the actual key I've got here.

356
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:22,980
You have got to be freaking kidding me!

357
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:30,200
It might be a key to another
pair of cuffs For all you know,

358
00:21:30,500 --> 00:21:31,560
cha-ba-ba-ba-ba!

359
00:21:33,380 --> 00:21:36,360
In this great tower of law.

360
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:40,797
There are five members
of CP9, including me.

361
00:21:40,880 --> 00:21:43,777
And each and every member
has a very own need.

362
00:21:43,860 --> 00:21:46,500
So let's get in the game, hide and seek.

363
00:21:48,260 --> 00:21:51,037
So you're saying we gotta
beat each one of you guys.

364
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:53,397
And then try every key on our handcuffs.

365
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:55,937
And that's the only way we're
gonna find the real one.

366
00:21:56,020 --> 00:21:57,837
What a stupid way to keep us busy.

367
00:21:57,920 --> 00:22:00,477
While we're wasting time
on your key hunting game.

368
00:22:00,560 --> 00:22:02,677
Your chief is gonna
escape through those gates

369
00:22:02,760 --> 00:22:05,397
with Rob retrieving Robin
is our first priority?

370
00:22:05,480 --> 00:22:10,245
If we focus on getting Robin back first,
we can worry about the key is afterward.

371
00:22:10,520 --> 00:22:13,402
Let's just ignore that
weirdo and start searching

372
00:22:15,360 --> 00:22:19,700
Hey, you've got some brains,
but I'm afraid if you do that,

373
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:22,037
then you'll leave me with no choice?

374
00:22:22,120 --> 00:22:24,220
I'll toss this kid to the ocean!

375
00:22:27,380 --> 00:22:30,157
We're kind enough to give
you guys a sporting chance.

376
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:31,070
See ya.

377
00:22:31,560 --> 00:22:33,500
Hey, get back here!

378
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:35,630
Hold on, Luffy.

379
00:22:35,713 --> 00:22:37,320
Will you just wait a second?

380
00:22:39,180 --> 00:22:41,340
Stop running and listen to me.

381
00:22:41,480 --> 00:22:44,715
Let's decide what we're going
to do before we split up.

382
00:22:44,960 --> 00:22:46,780
Shut up and let me go!

383
00:22:47,360 --> 00:22:49,360
Get a hold of yourself, Straw Hat.

384
00:22:50,580 --> 00:22:52,800
I'm guessing Luchi's that pigeon guy.

385
00:22:53,340 --> 00:22:54,540
Yeah, that's him.

386
00:22:54,820 --> 00:22:58,477
From what that freak told us, he's the
only one they've got guarding Robin.

387
00:22:58,560 --> 00:23:00,854
Our best bet's to send Luffy after him.

388
00:23:01,220 --> 00:23:05,037
Luffy, since you're raring to go,
you can hunt down that pigeon guy.

389
00:23:05,120 --> 00:23:07,000
Where we go? Where we go?

390
00:23:07,360 --> 00:23:10,017
Excluding Luffy, we've
got a head count of six.

391
00:23:10,100 --> 00:23:13,220
He said there are only
five CP9 agents with keys.

392
00:23:13,520 --> 00:23:17,285
So I say we spread out, take them
down, and catch up with Luffy.

393
00:23:18,120 --> 00:23:21,197
If they drag her across those
gates, we'll never get her back!

394
00:23:21,280 --> 00:23:23,220
It's a race against time!

395
00:23:23,700 --> 00:23:25,120
Then let's get going!

396
00:23:28,300 --> 00:23:32,240
Take him down, or we die
trying. Yeah! Good luck!

397
00:23:34,960 --> 00:23:36,600
Go, pirate guys, go!

398
00:23:36,780 --> 00:23:38,040
You can do it!

399
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:39,790
Huh?

400
00:23:43,560 --> 00:23:45,060
Chimney? Gombe!

401
00:23:45,380 --> 00:23:47,660
Where did those two disappear to?

402
00:23:48,720 --> 00:23:51,000
They must have taken Robin this way!

403
00:23:51,240 --> 00:23:53,593
They couldn't have gotten too far ahead!

404
00:23:53,940 --> 00:23:57,940
I'm not gonna let them take you
through the Gates of Justice, Robin!

405
00:24:01,460 --> 00:24:03,800
There's no help for you, Nico Robin!

406
00:24:05,560 --> 00:24:07,717
You can keep wishing for them to come,

407
00:24:07,800 --> 00:24:11,153
but they'll never find their
way to the Gates of Justice!

408
00:24:12,560 --> 00:24:13,560
AHAHAHA, AHAHAHA!

409
00:24:15,560 --> 00:24:16,390
AHHHHH!

410
00:24:16,473 --> 00:24:19,037
QUIT HIDDING FROM ME,
YOU PIDGEON-LOVING JERK!

411
00:24:19,120 --> 00:24:21,677
I gotta find the kitchen
before I do any more fightin'!

412
00:24:21,760 --> 00:24:24,080
I'm in serious trouble if I don't...

413
00:24:25,100 --> 00:24:25,930
CUDABOO!

414
00:24:27,500 --> 00:24:30,817
I need a bottle and a half of
cola to properly fuel Cudaboo,

415
00:24:30,900 --> 00:24:33,937
and I've already managed to go through
a little more than two of them today!

416
00:24:34,020 --> 00:24:37,844
I gotta nab at least three full
bottles if I'm gonna take on CP9!

417
00:24:38,340 --> 00:24:39,820
Huh? There!

418
00:24:40,120 --> 00:24:41,826
That's got to be the kitchen!

419
00:24:51,680 --> 00:24:55,327
You've come face-to-face with
the gossip-loving silent Fukuro!

420
00:24:55,500 --> 00:24:57,420
I suppose you want my keys!

421
00:24:57,720 --> 00:25:00,920
Great, just move where I
can refill my cola! Zappa!

422
00:25:11,780 --> 00:25:13,040
No one in there.

423
00:25:17,340 --> 00:25:18,170
Nope.

424
00:25:20,720 --> 00:25:21,780
Not in there.

425
00:25:24,460 --> 00:25:25,480
I'm empty.

426
00:25:26,600 --> 00:25:27,740
What's the deal?

427
00:25:27,860 --> 00:25:29,742
I can't find anyone around here.

428
00:25:30,260 --> 00:25:31,720
Not that I really mind.

429
00:25:37,760 --> 00:25:40,231
Ah, so you're too afraid to freeze the m -

430
00:25:42,620 --> 00:25:43,800
It's not him!

431
00:25:49,600 --> 00:25:50,620
He's asleep?

432
00:25:51,760 --> 00:25:53,480
Is he with CP9?

433
00:25:55,380 --> 00:25:56,210
What?

434
00:25:56,380 --> 00:25:59,204
He just let the key out
while he's taking a nap?

435
00:25:59,600 --> 00:26:02,437
My luck couldn't possibly
be this good, could it?

436
00:26:02,520 --> 00:26:04,226
This is a golden opportunity.

437
00:26:05,600 --> 00:26:06,897
What is this place?

438
00:26:06,980 --> 00:26:09,039
It looks like some kind of dungeon.

439
00:26:17,320 --> 00:26:20,797
Your hopeless quest for
your friend's freedom

440
00:26:20,880 --> 00:26:25,037
has doomed you to die a
dreadful death by my hand!

441
00:26:25,120 --> 00:26:27,620
Do you hear my words?

442
00:26:27,800 --> 00:26:28,717
You're doomed.

443
00:26:28,800 --> 00:26:31,540
I said you're doomed. Doomed.

444
00:26:32,360 --> 00:26:33,720
Doomed. OOOJU!

445
00:26:36,300 --> 00:26:37,130
YOYOY!

446
00:26:41,160 --> 00:26:42,700
Geez, he's allowed.

447
00:26:43,160 --> 00:26:44,925
This room better not be empty!

448
00:26:48,160 --> 00:26:48,990
Damn it!

449
00:26:50,160 --> 00:26:51,748
Getting real tired of this.

450
00:27:00,140 --> 00:27:02,340
What's wrong? Just relax.

451
00:27:04,540 --> 00:27:05,740
Tell you what.

452
00:27:06,180 --> 00:27:07,760
I'll put on some tea.

453
00:27:22,340 --> 00:27:24,240
Well, that sounds wonderful.

454
00:27:34,360 --> 00:27:35,697
Your swords are drawn.

455
00:27:35,780 --> 00:27:37,015
You don't waste time!

456
00:27:38,800 --> 00:27:41,780
They've been thirsty
for the taste of blood?
